{
  "about": "Named proof shots for tools/proof/capture.mjs. Edit here, not in the script. Views place the camera from the boat's bow: az degrees clockwise from the bow (180 = astern, 90 = starboard beam), dist and h in metres for our 3 m kayak (bigger boats scale up), fov in degrees (small = long lens), look = aim this many metres above the boat. Sea numbers are open-Atlantic targets from creative/sailor-realism-checklist.md (WMO Beaufort table); cloud and wind are looks, not physics. heel = [beat, reach, run] degrees for sailing yachts in that wind (Sam's targets; the replay's sail plan is not changed). maxHeel: a still waits (up to 1.5 s) for a yacht's roll to come inside this many degrees. A view with toward: moon looks along the moon's bearing.",
